  "verbalization": "Diflunisal, a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID), is linked to Rheumatoid Arthritis through a chain of indications that involve osteoarthritis and other conditions. The evidence suggests that Diflunisal may exert its therapeutic effects on osteoarthritis, which in turn could influence the development or progression of Rheumatoid Arthritis. This pathway is supported by the presence of multiple indirect links, including the indication of Diflunisal for osteoarthritis, and the subsequent indications for piroxicam and tiaprofenic acid, both of which are also NSAIDs. The shared mechanism of action—reducing inflammation and pain—may contribute to the potential relationship between Diflunisal and Rheumatoid Arthritis, though the exact causal pathway remains unclear. The evidence highlights a possible role of NSAIDs in the pathogenesis of rheumatic diseases, but further research is needed to establish a definitive link.",
